.nh
.TH "TEAMS" "1" "Oct 2026" "teams dev" "teams Manual"

.SH NAME
teams-doctor - Check the config, token store, scopes, clock and Graph reachability


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBteams doctor [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Diagnose the local setup and print the fix for every problem.

.PP
doctor checks the config file, the token store (including keychain
reachability), the scopes the current token carries against the feature
matrix, the clock skew against Graph's own clock, and Graph reachability.
It never makes a write call; --offline skips the network checks entirely.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for doctor

.PP
\fB--offline\fP[=false]
	skip the checks that need the network


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	machine-readable JSON output

.PP
\fB--no-color\fP[=false]
	disable colours (also honours NO_COLOR)

.PP
\fB--no-input\fP[=false]
	never prompt; fail fast instead

.PP
\fB--profile\fP=""
	profile to use (default: the configured default_profile)

.PP
\fB--quiet\fP[=false]
	suppress progress messages on stderr

.PP
\fB--read-only\fP[=false]
	refuse write commands

.PP
\fB-v\fP, \fB--verbose\fP[=0]
	verbose diagnostics on stderr (-v, -vv)


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBteams(1)\fP
